  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">VIV&#xc1; MORER&#xc9;: SMALL ISLAND. BROAD HORIZONS - IMPROVE ACCESS TO EDUCATION AND PROFESSIONAL SKILLS, AND THE PROMOTION OF ENVIRONMENT SUSTAINABILITY FOR 1</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Viv&#xe1; Morer&#xe9;: Small Island. Broad Horizons project in the Island of Boipeba, Municipality of Cairu, Bahia, Brazil aims to support access to information and create initiatives related to human rights, access to resources, financial and environmental issues and: gender equality with the local community, especially the most marginalized groups, by offering several types of support to the participants such as workshops, seminars, internships, long-term courses, a community library, a community garden, dialogue circles, assemblies, a community run coffee shop, a women&#xb4;s cooperative, and a community thrift-store among other outreach projects.</narrative>
  </description>
